    "story": "They always gather when I come through. Every whistle echoes different between the boards. Red paint holds the heat, smoke folds low. These streets know the sound of me. Crossing timbers click sharper in towns like this. Closer. Personal. I don’t run faster here. Just prouder.",
    "notes": "The architectural framing creates a cinematic “reveal,” positioning the train as both subject and performer. The buildings provide rhythm and scale — the strong verticals amplify the horizontal force of the engine. Heim’s tonal control and slightly desaturated palette nod to early Kodachrome prints without mimicking their palette. This piece invites storytelling: about place, about return, about what still turns heads when it arrives.",
