    "story": "Right on time. Sure hope Aunt May’s on this one. Don’t want to be late for dinner — she never lets you forget it. Can’t wait to hear her stories. Bet she brought that old box of letters again… just to make us cry all over the good pie.",
    "notes": "This image blends compositional strength with narrative softness. The centered figures act as both characters and emotional anchors — they don’t just witness the train’s passage, they complete the moment. The billowing steam draws the eye upward, while the shallow curve of the track bends time itself. Heim’s painterly restraint keeps the tones grounded, with subtle contrast in the coats and surrounding earth. Reminiscent of mid-century American realism, the piece invites slow reading: it’s a frame from a larger memory, shared by those who’ve waited and those who still do.",
